Z||000003||87FieroGTx||11-13-2001||01:09 AM|||| Just stroking the engine will only give you 20hp "I" Don't think it's worth the $$. It cost me $1,800 I did most of the work) to rebuild my 2.8 to a 3.2 with 200hp, I think you could get a 3.4 from a Camaro and rebuild that, all you need to do to get it to fit is have starter holes drilled. <P> The 3.4 is only rated at 160 hp but they have MUCH more torque than our 2.8's and for say $500 you could get them to 220hp<P>If I was you I would go for a built 3.4.  <P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75+ shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.9 13.5 1/4||||reg||1
Z||000004||DKOV||11-13-2001||02:55 PM||||a 3.4 SINGLE Over Head Cam, you mean...<P>The 3.4 DUAL (or twin) Over Head Cam engines base line HP is 215.  With some "minor" mods and 300 HP is not out of reach.<P>Plenty of Torque and plenty of high end (7500 + RPM) horse power.<P>In my opinion, the very best package  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
